{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggBRf81s7bqopG2RBRZz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Fixed: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so the shares add back up to the full 1 zł.\n\n**The cause:** `total // people` throws away the remainder. The fix in `money.py` uses `divmod`, then gives the leftover grosze one each to the first people in the list. That way no two shares differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests:** I added two to `test_money.py` and watched both fail before changing the code:\n- `100 / 3` must give `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- For every total from 0 to 249 and 1 to 11 people, the shares must add up to the total and differ by at most 1.\n\nAll 5 tests now pass with `python3 -m unittest`. The project has no linter or build step set up, so there was nothing else to run.\n\n**Two things to know:**\n- **Who pays the extra grosz:** it always goes to whoever is first in the list. If the same person always ends up first, they'll always pay it. If you want it spread fairly over time, rotate the order or pick at random, but that's your call.\n- **No independent review:** your workflow asks for a `reviewer` subagent, but none is set up in this environment, so this fix hasn't been reviewed by anyone else."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":538,"cache_read_input_tokens":20523,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":538},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f376b56e-e5be-48f3-a835-3bbb632ee43c","uuid":"46706b8f-1254-4f6e-ab09-ee14c3bca9af","timestamp":"2026-11-03T14:49:53.570Z","request_id":"req_011CggBRetP8Yymgx2gwkeMW"}
